# Smallest correct change

The best Later feature is one we did not build.

1. Need this for V1? If Later/TBD, stop.
2. Already in the repo? Reuse.
3. Stdlib / Next / Supabase already does it? Use that.
4. Would this slow A1 or A4 (query, bundle, Realtime)? Reject that shape.
5. Then write the minimum that keeps isolation + the happy path.

No extra abstractions, no second state/date/CSS library, fewest files. Fix the shared function once (authz, scoped query), not every caller.

```ts
// ❌ disappearing posts — P2
if (post.expiresAt) hide(post)

// ✅ omit
```

Mark a known perf ceiling: `// perf: full list until >50 rows; virtualize if A1 grows`.
